# openOODA WebAssembly Backend State — 2026-08-26

Logline: One-shot inventory of the WASM emit-wasm backend; 20 modules, 3,218 lines, structural parity with x86 features, and the gaps that keep it from being a complete backend.

Setup: Reads ooda/oodac/wasm_*.oo (20 files). Line counts from `wc -l`. No compiler run. No file edits. No /tmp writes. The WASM lane is outside the lane discipline (wasm_emit_* files are not edited); this audit is read-only.

Beats:
  1. List every WASM module with line count and one-line role.
  2. Map x86 emit modules to WASM equivalents and mark parity.
  3. Rank the gaps by impact on a complete WASM backend.
  4. State recommendations and the next 3 actions.

File: openOODA/audit/wasm-backend-state.oot
Status: smoke — read-only final audit, 2026-08-26
Scope: emit-wasm (ooda/oodac/wasm_*.oo); wasm_direct_emit.oo is the side driver.

---

## 1. WASM modules

20 modules, 3,218 lines (`wc -l oodac/wasm_*.oo`). `wasm_backend_driver.oo` is the 50-line top entry that ties tokenize, parse, and AST-module build. Every module has the 4-element Academy header.

| # | Module | Lines | Description |
|---|--------|-------|-------------|
| 1 | wasm_backend_driver.oo | 50 | Top entry; tokenize, AST-parse, dispatch to WASI, browser, or standalone module build; writes .wasm file. |
| 2 | wasm_direct_emit.oo | 19 | Side driver `emit-wasm`; calls backend driver with `wasi` target; returns bool success (does not write file). |
| 3 | wasm_opcodes.oo | 143 | WebAssembly 1.0 binary opcode and section ID constants; control, local, memory, numeric, conversion. |
| 4 | wasm_types.oo | 86 | Value types (i32, i64, f32, f64, externref, funcref); function type signature encoding and equality. |
| 5 | wasm_leb128.oo | 125 | LEB128 variable-length codec; u32/u64/i32/i64 encode and decode; pure arithmetic. |
| 6 | wasm_binary_builder.oo | 231 | Module builder; type, import, function, memory, export, code, data sections; LEB128 framing; valid flat byte stream. |
| 7 | wasm_mem_layout.oo | 209 | 4-tier linear memory model (scratch, rodata, shadow stack, heap); string literal dedup, malloc with memory.grow, memcpy, memset. |
| 8 | wasm_arc_runtime.oo | 245 | ARC reference counting runtime; 8-byte header ABI, retain, release, scope exit drops, reassign drop, get_refcount, get_flags. |
| 9 | wasm_cap_lowering.oo | 195 | Capability lowering and sandboxing; 20+ cap tokens recognised, cap subsumption table, fail-closed syscall grant check, zero-cost dummy. |
| 10 | wasm_target_wasi.oo | 176 | WASI preview 1 target; fd_write, fd_read, clock_time_get, random_get, proc_exit imports; stdout print, file read/write, now_ms, proc_exit lowering. |
| 11 | wasm_target_browser.oo | 231 | Browser / WUI target; env.wui_host_patch, env.wui_host_log imports; wui_init, wui_on_event, wui_get_patch_ptr, wui_get_patch_len exports. |
| 12 | wasm_lower_fn.oo | 211 | Function and module lowering; collect signatures, lower params and locals, tail-position return, WASI `_start` and start entry. |
| 13 | wasm_lower_expr.oo | 255 | Expression lowering; ELitInt, ELitFloat, ELitBool, EVar, EBinop, EUnop, EIf, ECall, EMethod, AstBlock; alloc, f64 lit encode. |
| 14 | wasm_lower_stmt.oo | 125 | Statement lowering; SLet, SLetMut, SAssign, SReturn, SExpr, SBreak, SContinue; type map, break/continue depth resolution. |
| 15 | wasm_lower_control.oo | 245 | Structured control flow; if/else, while, for, match; labeled break/continue, match arm pattern dispatch, expr-or-block. |
| 16 | wasm_lower_adt.oo | 213 | Result[T,E] and Option[T] lowering; Ok/Err/Some/None tagged linear memory cells; is_ok, is_err, is_some, is_none, unwrap methods. |
| 17 | wasm_lower_list.oo | 65 | List[T] lowering; new, len, get, push. **list_push is a no-op** (drops the value); list_new returns scratch 0. |
| 18 | wasm_lower_struct.oo | 74 | Struct memory lowering; field offsets, field get/set, struct inst. **struct_inst is a no-op** (evaluates fields and returns scratch i32). |
| 19 | wasm_lower_string.oo | 247 | UTF-8 string and RODATA; str lit, len, byte_at, eq, ne, concat, slice; 12-byte header, heap bump alloc, byte copy loops. |
| 20 | wasm_lower_ops.oo | 73 | Binop and unop wrappers; short-circuit &&, ||; arithmetic, bitwise, comparison for i32, i64, f64; Neg, Not. |

**Smoke coverage.** `ooda/scripts/wasm_*.oo` has 174 dedicated smoke scripts (vs x86 smoke count of similar order). The `wasm_*.oo` modules are not paired one-to-one with smokes; the smoke naming follows the language-shape under test, not the lowering module. `test_wasm_caps.oo` (lines 1-15) is the only in-tree fixture shipped to validate the cap surface.

**Line distribution.** 2 modules hit the 256-line cap exactly (wasm_lower_expr.oo at 255 is within cap; wasm_target_browser.oo at 231, wasm_target_wasi.oo at 176, wasm_arc_runtime.oo at 245 are all comfortably under). No overflow.

---

## 2. x86 vs WASM parity

46 x86 modules, 20 WASM modules. The two backends have a different shape: x86 is token-folding with one arm per source shape; WASM is AST-direct with one module per lowering phase. The parity table is by **feature** (one x86 arm vs one WASM lowering entry), not by file name.

| # | x86 module | WASM | Status |
|---|------------|------|--------|
| 1 | x86_emit.oo | Y | wasm_backend_driver.oo (50 lines); both are top entry. WASM lacks the 4-gate pre-dispatch (contract / secret / diag / refuse) and the per-arm wrote counter. |
| 2 | x86_emit_alu.oo | Y | wasm_lower_expr.oo EBinop + wasm_lower_ops.oo; i32 / i64 / f64. Same operator surface, no width/atom fold. |
| 3 | x86_emit_bind.oo | inline | wasm_lower_stmt.oo SLet and SAssign; folded into statement lowering. |
| 4 | x86_emit_contract.oo | - | No WASM contract gate; openOODA contract annotations are unchecked at the WASM surface. |
| 5 | x86_emit_ctl.oo | Y | wasm_lower_control.oo if/else/while/for; both fold const branches. |
| 6 | x86_emit_diag.oo | - | No WASM typed diagnostic reporter; backend driver returns "ERR\twasm_driver\t..." strings only. |
| 7 | x86_emit_elf.oo | Y (alt) | wasm_binary_builder.oo; Wasm binary not ELF. Different format, same role (final framing). |
| 8 | x86_emit_float.oo | Y | wasm_lower_expr.oo ELitFloat; f64 const encode via IEEE-754 bit pattern. |
| 9 | x86_emit_float_routine.oo | inline | Folded into wasm_target_wasi.oo fd_write path. |
| 10 | x86_emit_fn.oo | Y | wasm_lower_fn.oo; supports any arity (WASM local.get / local.set, no register class). |
| 11 | x86_emit_fold.oo | - | No WASM hello.oo greet fold; WasmConstant strings go through RODATA + fd_write directly. |
| 12 | x86_emit_for.oo | Y | wasm_lower_control.oo wasm_lower_for. |
| 13 | x86_emit_frame.oo | - | No WASM frame manager needed; structured control flow removes the SysV stp/ldp prologue. |
| 14 | x86_emit_free.oo | - | No WASM freelist allocator; wasm_mem_layout.oo has bump allocator only, no free. |
| 15 | x86_emit_greet.oo | inline | Folded into wasm_target_wasi.oo fd_write. |
| 16 | x86_emit_harv.oo | - | No WASM harvest walker; WASM consumes the typed AST directly. |
| 17 | x86_emit_heap.oo | Y (alt) | wasm_mem_layout.oo heap; sys_mmap 9/222 vs memory.grow 0x40. |
| 18 | x86_emit_int.oo | Y | wasm_lower_expr.oo ELitInt; i32.const / i64.const. |
| 19 | x86_emit_list.oo | partial | wasm_lower_list.oo exists but `list_push` is a `drop` no-op; `list_new` returns 0. **stub** (not a real runtime). |
| 20 | x86_emit_loop.oo | Y | wasm_lower_control.oo wasm_lower_while. |
| 21 | x86_emit_match.oo | Y | wasm_lower_control.oo wasm_lower_match + wasm_lower_adt.oo; 2-arm only; no 3-arm path. |
| 22 | x86_emit_multi.oo | - | No WASM multi-module separate compilation; single .wasm per source. |
| 23 | x86_emit_mut.oo | inline | Folded into wasm_lower_stmt.oo SLetMut and SAssign. |
| 24 | x86_emit_no_output.oo | - | No WASM post-emit run-time check; the `_start` wrapper has no `<name>: no-output` sentinel. |
| 25 | x86_emit_opt.oo | Y | wasm_lower_adt.oo Option[T]; same 16-byte cell layout. |
| 26 | x86_emit_r89.oo (5-6 args) | inline | Folded into wasm_lower_fn.oo param lowering. |
| 27 | x86_emit_rcx.oo (4 args) | inline | Folded into wasm_lower_fn.oo. |
| 28 | x86_emit_rdx.oo (3 args) | inline | Folded into wasm_lower_fn.oo. |
| 29 | x86_emit_rec.oo | inline | Folded into wasm_lower_fn.oo; recursive call via wasm_env_lookup_func. |
| 30 | x86_emit_rsi.oo (2 args) | inline | Folded into wasm_lower_fn.oo. |
| 31 | x86_emit_secret.oo | - | No WASM SECRET gate; taint tracking absent at the WASM surface. |
| 32 | x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo | - | No WASM 5-shape refuse gate; silent fall-through is the norm (see x86-final.oot §2 #3). |
| 33 | x86_emit_span.oo | - | No WASM ALU-atom + width fold. |
| 34 | x86_emit_str.oo | Y | wasm_lower_string.oo; concat, len, byte_at, eq, ne, slice; 12-byte header. |
| 35 | x86_emit_struct.oo | partial | wasm_lower_struct.oo exists but `wasm_lower_struct_inst` does not allocate, just evaluates fields and returns scratch i32. **stub**. |
| 36 | x86_emit_sys.oo | Y (alt) | wasm_target_wasi.oo; sys_write 1 / sys_exit 60 vs fd_write / proc_exit. |
| 37 | x86_emit_typed_let.oo | inline | Folded into wasm_lower_stmt.oo SLet. |
| 38 | x86_emit_walk.oo | - | No WASM println-const harvest walker. |
| 39 | x86_runtime.oo | Y (alt) | wasm_arc_runtime.oo; ARC reference counting vs x86 zero-libc runtime registry. |
| 40 | x86_ssa_compile.oo | - | No WASM SSA pipeline; WASM uses direct AST lowering (matches aarch64). |
| 41 | x86_ssa_emit.oo | - | Same. |
| 42 | x86_ssa_emit_float.oo | - | Same. |
| 43 | x86_ssa_emit_remap.oo | - | Same. |
| 44 | x86_ast_handlers.oo | - | No WASM typed-AST handler ladder. |
| 45 | x86_ast_nodes.oo | - | Same. |
| 46 | x86_ast_typed.oo | - | Same; WASM uses `ast.oo` directly via wasm_ast_args / ast_tag / ast_is. |

**Parity.** 25 of 46 (54%) have a WASM equivalent (Y, Y-alt, or inline). 2 have a partial equivalent (List, struct; both are stubs in practice). 19 have no equivalent. Treating the 4 SSA + 3 typed-AST files as one pipeline cluster (because WASM and aarch64 both use direct AST lowering, the role is covered), the structural gap is 12 missing ports.

Per-area rollup:
- ALU / arith: 1 of 1 — full parity (EBinop + binop helpers).
- Memory / heap: 1 of 2 — heap present (memory.grow bump), no free.
- Control flow: 4 of 4 — full parity (if, while, for, match 2-arm).
- Types / data: 3 of 5 — Option, typed-let, String present; List and struct are stubs.
- Functions: 5 of 5 — full parity (rsi/rdx/rcx/r89/fn all inline in wasm_lower_fn.oo).
- Float: 2 of 2 — full parity (ELitFloat + fd_write).
- ADT: 1 of 1 — full parity (Result + Option via wasm_lower_adt.oo).
- ARC: 1 of 1 — full parity (wasm_arc_runtime.oo).
- Contracts / secret: 0 of 2 — both absent at the WASM surface.
- Diag / error / refuse: 0 of 3 — diag, no_output, and shape_refuse all absent.
- Pipeline: 0 of 8 — SSA and typed-AST pipelines absent (consistent with aarch64).
- Multi-module: 0 of 1 — single .wasm per source.
- Target binding: 2 of 2 — WASI and browser targets both present (browser residual per SHIPPED.oot).

---

## 3. Gaps (ranked by impact on a complete WASM backend)

1. **WASM is NOT at PASS.** `openOODA/SHIPPED.oot` declares: "Not a complete WASM backend." `wasm_lower_list.oo:60-64` (`list_push` drops the value) and `wasm_lower_struct.oo:19-34` (struct inst returns scratch i32 without allocation) are the two confirmed stubs. The backend compiles hello.oo, single-fn println of literals, const-arith println, const-if-true/if-false, and const-comparison only. List push, struct allocation, multi-fn call, control flow with non-const conditions, and 3-arm match all stay unbuilt.
2. **List[T] runtime is a stub (wasm_lower_list.oo:60-64).** `wasm_lower_list_push` is `wasm_env_emit(env, op_drop()); return l_ty;` — the appended value is discarded. `wasm_lower_list_new` returns i32.const 0. Any source that does `let xs: List[Int] = [1, 2, 3]; println(xs[0])` will read from offset 0 of memory, which holds the heap-ptr, not the first element. HIGH. ~150 lines to add capacity tracking, growth, and get/set with the 8-byte header layout that wasm_mem_layout.oo already implies.
3. **Struct allocation is a stub (wasm_lower_struct.oo:19-34).** `wasm_lower_struct_inst` walks the field values, calls wasm_lower_expr on each (which emits and drops the result), and returns a scratch i32. No malloc, no ARC retain, no field stores. Field get/set (rows 36-39 in the parity table) are correct because they only need a pointer + offset, but the pointer is never a real struct pointer. HIGH. ~120 lines to allocate via wasm_mem_layout.oo + wasm_arc_runtime.oo and store each field at the documented offsets.
4. **No refuse / no-output / contract / secret / diag gates at the WASM entry.** `wasm_backend_driver.oo:26-33` does tokenize, parse, then dispatch with no pre-flight. Any source that fails the 5-shape refuse gate on x86 (Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]) will silently miscompile on WASM. HIGH (per audit/x86-final.oot §2 #3 which names this exact gap as a cross-lane HIGH risk). ~240 lines, mirrors x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo:21-30+ wired at wasm_backend_driver.oo:29-32.
5. **3-arm match path is absent (wasm_lower_control.oo:135-181).** `wasm_lower_match_arm` is recursive but the comment in `aarch64-final-state.oot §3 #1` lists 3-arm match as one of the 5 hostile shapes. The WASM path exists in principle but is not exercised. MEDIUM. ~80 lines.
6. **No multi-module separate compilation (wasm_lower_fn.oo:146-207).** `wasm_compile_ast_module` builds one .wasm per `wasm_driver_build_file` call; two .oo files cannot be linked into one .wasm. x86 has x86_emit_multi.oo for `.globl` + extern call sites; WASM has no equivalent. MEDIUM. ~100 lines.
7. **No ARC integration at lowering sites.** `wasm_arc_runtime.oo` provides `wasm_arc_emit_retain`, `wasm_arc_emit_release`, `wasm_arc_emit_scope_drops`, `wasm_arc_emit_return_drops` (lines 99-205), but no lowering call site invokes them. Every String, List, Result, and struct allocation is leaked. MEDIUM. ~50 lines per lowering call site, ~5 sites.
8. **Capability framework is declared but unwired.** `wasm_cap_lowering.oo` has 20+ cap tokens, a subsumption table, `wasm_assert_syscall_granted` (line 136), and `wasm_extract_caps_from_params` (line 147). None of these are called from wasm_lower_fn.oo or wasm_target_wasi.oo. Sandbox violations in the WASM lane do not fail-closed at compile time. MEDIUM. ~30 lines to wire at wasm_lower_fn.oo:43-118.
9. **Browser target is residual (wasm_target_browser.oo).** Per `openOODA/SHIPPED.oot`: "A browser WASM host is residual. Not a complete WASM backend." Browser compile path exists; the host page that consumes `wui_init` / `wui_on_event` / `wui_get_patch_ptr` does not. RESIDUAL. No backend work needed; host page is a separate lane.
10. **No SSA / typed-AST pipeline.** Consistent with aarch64. RESIDUAL. x86 SSA is itself under fix (per audit/x86-final.oot §2 #4); porting the unsound pipeline is not net-positive. Re-evaluate after SSA lands.

---

## 4. Recommendations

**Verdict.** The WASM backend is **PARTIAL** by structure and **NOT at PASS** by status. The 20 modules cover the full feature surface at the AST-lowering level, but the runtime stubs (List push, struct alloc, ARC) and the missing safety gates (refuse, no_output, contract, secret, diag) keep the lane in the same shape as the aarch64 lane before the refuse gate landed. 174 dedicated smoke scripts under `ooda/scripts/wasm_*.oo` exercise the const-fold surface (println, int, arith, if-true/if-false, comparison, concat) but do not touch List push, struct inst, or 3-arm match.

**Recommended next 3 actions, ranked by impact:**
1. **Replace `wasm_lower_list.oo:60-64` with a real `wasm_lower_list_push`.** Allocate 12-byte header + (len + 1) * elem_size bytes via `wasm_mem_layout.oo::wasm_emit_malloc`, store the slot, store the element, and bump the length. Also fix `wasm_lower_list_new` to allocate the empty header. Closes the List empty-stdout cluster (per `x86-final.oot` row 12, 80.1% of 202 fixtures). Estimated: ~150 lines.
2. **Replace `wasm_lower_struct.oo:19-34` with a real `wasm_lower_struct_inst`.** Use the documented 8-byte ARC header + 4-byte field layout (line 21 comment). Allocate via bump, init ARC header via `wasm_arc_emit_init_header` (line 40), store each field at the right offset. Then add a `wasm_lower_struct_let` that emits `local.tee` of the struct pointer. Closes the struct empty-stdout cluster (per `x86-final.oot` row 11, 80.8% of 277 fixtures). Estimated: ~120 lines.
3. **Add a 5-shape refuse gate at `wasm_backend_driver.oo:29-32` (or split to a new `wasm_emit_shape_refuse.oo`).** Mirror `x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo:21-30+` for Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]. Wire between the AST parse at line 28 and the dispatch at line 30. Closes the cross-lane HIGH risk named in `audit/x86-ast-typed-shim.oot:74`. Estimated: ~240 lines, mostly mirror.

After these three land, the WASM lane reaches structural parity with the x86 post-fix surface (per `audit/x86-final.oot` §1) and the hostile-probe floor can be re-measured for WASM. The 174 existing smoke scripts under `ooda/scripts/wasm_*.oo` provide a baseline; the next-mile smokes should cover List push, struct field store, and 3-arm match. Multi-module and browser host stay residual for a later wave.

---

*End of audit. Next agent: pick up action #1 (List runtime) or action #4 (refuse gate), depending on the lane discipline of the day.*
